Two instances are extant, one with annotations (ID:4423) one without (ID:4428).</note><idno type="APIS">4424</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work4427"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mngon par rtogs pa'i bshad pa</title><title xml:lang="bo">མངོན་པར་རྟོགས་པའི་བཤད་པ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpal mngon par rtogs pa'i dka' ba’i gnas bshad pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpal mngon par rtogs pa'i bshad pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpal mngon par rtogs pa'i dka' ba'i gnas bshad pa lo tsA ba rin chen bzang pos mdzad pa bzhugs</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mngon par rtogs pa'i dka' gnad</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpal mngon par rtogs pa'i dka' gnad</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1042-01-01" notAfter="1054-12-31">after 1042 before 1054</date><author ref="person:3784">rin chen bzang po</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Rin chen bzang po is reporting the teaching of Atiśa (ID:3745) on the Śrī-(Cakrasaṃvara-)Abhisamaya. The text refers to the words of the Cakrasaṃvara-Abhisamaya. The explanations find parallels in Atiśa’s Abhisamayavibhaṅga (ID: 6213) (see &lt;&lt;Kano and Kawasaki 2014 [IWEZ79V4]&gt;&gt; for cross-references).</note><idno type="APIS">4427</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work4431"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bde ba can gyi smon lam</title><title xml:lang="bo">བདེ་བ་ཅན་གྱི་སྨོན་ལམ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bde can smon lam</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bde can zhing gi smon lam</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bde ba can gyi smon lam</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bDe ba can gyi smon lam</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="0996-01-01">after 996</date><author ref="person:3784">rin chen bzang po</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Prayer for Sukhavatī in verses of 9 syllables. Assuming the place of composition stands for Tho ling, composed between 996 (foundation of the monastery) and 1055 (author's passing).</note><idno type="APIS">4431</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5333"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgyud sde'i spyi'i rnam par bzhag pa 'thad ldan lung gi rgyan gyis spras pa</title><title xml:lang="bo">རྒྱུད་སྡེའི་སྤྱིའི་རྣམ་པར་བཞག་པ་འཐད་ལྡན་ལུང་གི་རྒྱན་གྱིས་སྤྲས་པ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgyud sde spyi'i rnam par bzhag pa 'thad ldan lung gi rgyan gyis spras pa</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1000-01-01" notAfter="1055-12-31">after 1000 before 1055</date><author ref="person:3784">rin chen bzang po</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><idno type="APIS">5333</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5335"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dam tshig mdor bsdus pa</title><title xml:lang="bo">དམ་ཚིག་མདོར་བསྡུས་པ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gdams pa dam tshig mdor bsdus pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon rin chen bzang pos gsungs pa'i dam tshig mdor bsdus bstan pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon rin chen bzang pos gsungs pa'i dam tshig mdor bsdus ba bstan pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sdom pa dam tshig mdor bsdus pa</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="0968-01-01" notAfter="1055-12-31">after 968 before 1055</date><author ref="person:4593">Anonymous</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">The title "sdom pa dam tshig mdor bsdus pa" is reported in [2PUVZG5F]: 46.&#13;
A post-colophon addition in (ID:5334) reports that the teaching of that text was requested by "rngos" (whom a gloss in dbu can identifies as "mar ston") from "lca/lba ston jo dga'" (lca/lba ston jo dga' la rngos ‹mar ston› kyis mnyan zhus nan tan bgyis so). Dan Martin (who reads "lba ston") notes "There was a Jo-dga' in the western Tibetan royal lineage whose lifespan could have coincided with Rinchen Zangpo's (Roerich’s Blue Annals, p. 38)" ([F8AC4NRI]). See [R894SIKE]: 63 for the reference to "jo dga'".</note><idno type="APIS">5335</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5624"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">pratiṣṭhāvidhi</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rab tu gnas pa'i cho ga</title><author ref="person:5625">ānandagarbha</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">D2523</note><idno type="APIS">5624</idno></bibl></listBibl><listPlace><place xml:id="place6216"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tho ling</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">ཐོ་ལིང</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">thon mthing gi gtsug lag khang</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">mtho lding</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">tho gling</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">mtho lding gser gyi lha khang</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">mtho lding rdo rje gdan</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">mtho lding dgon pa</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">dpal dpe med lhun gyis grub pa</placeName><location><geo>31.48314909153566 79.79735820745925</geo></location><idno type="APIS">6216</idno></place></listPlace><listRelation><relation xml:id="rel7307" name="student-of" active="#person3784" passive="#person3745" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel7408" name="lineage-predecessor-of" active="#person8218" passive="#person3784" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel4069" name="student-of" active="#person3784" passive="#person5639" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel523" name="author-of" active="#person3784" passive="#work4422" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel526" name="author-of" active="#person3784" passive="#work4424" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel524" name="author-of" active="#person3784" passive="#work4427" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel4028" name="translator-of" active="#person3784" passive="#work3701" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel7409" name="lineage-predecessor-of" active="#person3784" passive="#person8185" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel4063" name="translator-of" active="#person3784" passive="#work5624" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel4023" name="active-at" active="#person3784" passive="#place6216" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex1052023-04-241330"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel1077" name="author-of" active="#person3784" passive="#work5333" type="uncertain"/><relation xml:id="rel527" name="author-of" active="#person3784" passive="#work4431" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex1052023-04-241330"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel5648" name="records-the-teaching-of" active="#work5335" passive="#person3784" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel2922" name="student-of" active="#person3788" passive="#person3784" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel2593" name="student-of" active="#person6189" passive="#person3784" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel3518" name="composed-at" active="#work4431" passive="#place6216" type="uncertain"/></listRelation></standOff><text>
